{
  "requirement": "A definition glob MUST match a complete full name. `*` MUST match zero or more characters, including dots; all other valid name characters MUST match literally. An empty glob MUST be invalid. Every definition selection MUST use this matching rule, including requirements evidence inputs, CLI definition filters, and the authoring `references` tool, and MUST match against both requirements and named examples.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met.** The one weakness is that some test coverage is not marked `{test}` on this requirement (see Tests).\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/definition_glob.rs` `matches` is a dynamic-programming matcher over the whole name. `*` matches zero or more bytes, including dots. Every other byte must match literally. The match is anchored at both ends, so it is a complete-full-name match.\n- `validate` rejects an empty glob. It also rejects any character outside `[A-Za-z0-9._-*]`. That is the same alphabet `valid_name` in `src/lib.rs` allows (alphanumerics, `_`, `-`, and `.` as the segment separator) plus `*`, so \"all other valid name characters match literally\" holds.\n- Every selection site uses this shared module and filters out terms, so a selection matches both requirements and named examples:\n  - `InputSelector::resolve` in `src/inputs.rs` validates and then matches for requirements evidence inputs. It reports an error when nothing matches.\n  - `source_input` in `src/authoring/inputs.rs` applies the same match when checking read access.\n  - `status_markdown_with_options` and `info_markdown` in `src/commands.rs` are the CLI definition filters. Both validate the glob, match it, and report an error when nothing matches.\n  - The authoring `references` tool in `src/authoring/tools.rs` validates the selection. It uses `matches` for the definitions list, the reference sites and the anchors.\n- A search for other glob or `*` handling in `src` found no divergent matcher. All of these sites carry `{impl}` markers for this requirement, and I found no unmarked code that does selection matching.\n- I found no behavior beyond the requirement. The \"no match\" errors are specified by the CLI and input requirements, not by this one.\n\n**Tests**\n- The unit test in `src/definition_glob.rs` (`wildcard_crosses_dot_segments_and_matches_the_whole_name`) checks:\n  - `*` crossing dots;\n  - prefix anchoring (`prefix.foo.x.bar` does not match);\n  - a trailing `.*` requiring the dot (`foo.bar` does not match `foo.bar.*`);\n  - an empty glob being invalid;\n  - an unsupported character (`[`) being invalid.\n- The `tests/commands.rs` tests drive the real CLI:\n  - `commands_report_invalid_arguments_and_unmatched_selectors` checks an invalid glob for both `info` and `status`, and unmatched globs. It also checks that `requirements.*ready` matches both `requirements.ready` and `requirements.xready` (`*` matching zero characters) and excludes `requirements.pending`.\n  - `verbose_status_lists_fixme_judgments_and_globs_scope_issue_groups` checks that exact names, including an example, scope the output.\n  - `status_preserves_repository_wide_rust_findings_in_every_form` runs `status` with and without a selection.\n- Related tests cover the other surfaces, though they are not `{test}`-marked on this requirement:\n  - `requirements_inputs_track_matched_declarations_in_full_name_order` in `src/evidence.rs` covers the `foo.*.bar` example, which matches both a requirement and an example.\n  - `references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs` in `src/authoring/tools.rs` covers `requirements.*`, an empty selection and an invalid selection.\n  - `requirements_reads_select_requirements_and_examples_but_not_definitions` in `src/authoring/tools.rs` covers the `habeas` tool's `requirements` form.\n  - `selections_match_requirements_and_examples_but_never_named_definitions` in `tests/definitions.rs` covers CLI and `add-input` selections.\n- Possible additions (not required for this judgment): a unit assertion for suffix-mismatch anchoring, and one that a bare exact name does not prefix-match. The matcher logic is simple and correct, so I do not treat these as gaps.",
  "inputs": [
